      "id": 1,
      "text": "Cosmopolis was platted in 1861 and is the oldest modern settlement in Grays Harbor County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmopolis%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name means “city of the world,” a meaning attributed by James Phillips in 1853.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmopolis%2C_Washington",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A lumber mill opened in 1881, grew into a major employer, and the town incorporated as a town in 1891.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmopolis%2C_Washington",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Northern Pacific Railway built a spur through Cosmopolis in 1892, linking it to Tacoma via a bridge over the Chehalis River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmopolis%2C_Washington",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Chehalis River’s mouth, where Cosmopolis sits, is an estuarine bay of the Pacific Ocean, giving the town a unique coastal geography.",
